{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Lacey's Spring homes are older rural properties that have weathered decades of Alabama humidity and heavy tree debris. When gutters have been chronically clogged, fascia boards take the damage. Water running behind gutters soaks into the wood, creating conditions for rot.</p>

<p>Rural homes sometimes have deferred maintenance — it's hard to keep up with everything on a large property. Fascia damage may have been accumulating for years before anyone notices.</p>

<p>Caught early, fascia repair is straightforward. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters and roof structure.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection for water damage, soft spots, and rot. For damaged sections, we remove gutters, cut out rotted wood, and install new fascia using quality materials designed for our humid climate.</p>

<p>Then we install seamless gutters designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot.</p>
{% endset %}

